gainst the role requirements Step 3 - Interview If shortlisted, you’ll be invited to share your experience and learn more about the role. As part of the interview process, we may take references and complete qualification and/or background checks. Step 4 - Offer If successful, we’ll send you a formal offer and guide you through the onboarding process. Step 5 - Prepare to start A member of our team will be available to support you as you get ready to join Adelaide University. We understand moving to a new workplace can be a big change, so we've created some practical tips to help you navigate the transition smoothly. Tips for a successful transition to AU Need adjustments? We’re committed to ensuring our recruitment process is accessible to everyone. If you require adjustments at any stage, please let us know and we’ll work with you to make sure you’re supported. Make a request First Nations Employment Adelaide University aspires to be a university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples and is committed to reconciliation. Our future strategies towards Indigenous advancement include a focus on elevated employment outcomes for First Nations Peoples, with the University’s new Enterprise Agreement including multiple targeted employment benefits and outcomes for First Nations Peoples. As a part of this commitment Adelaide University has a dedicated First Nations Employment Advisor whose role is to provide strategic direction, advise on processes and procedures, support existing staff in their professional development and as a touch point for First Nations people interested in employment opportunities at Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku. For a culturally safe and confidential conversation regarding First Nations Employment at Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku, please contact Alison Hughes, Senior First Nations Employment Advisor at first.nations.employment@adelaide.edu.au Our commitment to you We empower our people to bring their unique contributions to