n menu Working with Children Check Procedure Sponsorship Policy Open menu Sponsorship Procedure Staff Code of Conduct Student Administration Policy Open menu Academic Progress Procedure Examination Procedure Student Loans Procedure Timetable Procedure Student Code of Conduct Student Complaints and Appeals Policy Open menu Student Appeals Procedure Student Complaints Resolution Procedure Student Conduct Policy Open menu Student Misconduct Procedure Student Critical Incident Policy Open menu Student Critical Incident Response Procedure Student Health Assessment and Medical Leave Policy Open menu Student Health Assessment and Medical Leave Procedure Student Wellbeing and Safety Policy Open menu Student Wellbeing and Safety Procedure Reasonable Adjustment Procedure Supplier Code of Conduct Support for Students Policy Open menu Support for Students Procedure Sustainability Policy Travel Policy Open menu High-Risk Travel Procedure Staff and Visitor Travel Procedure Student Travel Procedure Volunteer Policy Open menu Volunteer Procedure Wellbeing and Safety Policy Open menu Contractor Safety Procedure Hazard Management Procedure Open menu Boating Protocol Chemical Safety Management Protocol Controlled Substances and Controlled Plants Protocol Diving Protocol Electrical Safety Management Protocol Fieldwork Safety Protocol Firearm Protocol First Aid Management Protocol Hazardous Manual Handling Protocol Ionising Radiation Safety Management Protocol Noise and Sound Protocol Plant Safety Protocol Psychosocial Safety Protocol Working Alone or in Isolation Protocol Workplace Monitoring Protocol Incident Management Procedure Injury Management Procedure Permit to Work Procedure Open menu Confined Space Protocol Fall Prevention Protocol Hot Work Protocol Wellbeing and Safety Training and Induction​ Procedure Wellbeing and Safety System Management and Review Procedure Work Integrated Learning Policy Open menu Work Integrated Learning Procedure Publications Support Open menu Technology Open menu Staff and student account access Getting connected Report an incident or concern Open menu Public Interest Disclosure Addressing gender based violence FAQs First Nations Open menu Tirkangkaku Place of Learning Building our pathway ahead together Footprint on Country Strong foundations Cultural spaces Teaching and learning University Glossary Sustainability Open menu Careers in sustainable development Sustainability in research Sustainability partners Sustainability on campus Rankings and recognition Careers at Adelaide University Together, let’s launch your future At Adelaide University, we’re building something extraordinary: a place where bold ideas thrive and passionate people come together to shape the future. Whether you're an educator, researcher or professional, your journey starts here. Join one of Australia’s largest universities and be part of a community that’s making a global impact. Current opportunities We’re looking for talented individuals who are ready to make a difference. Explore the wide range of opportunities in our academic, research and professional portfolios. Use our secure portal to browse current openings and apply online. View current opportunities Internal opportunities (staff login required) Expand all Take the next step - how to apply Applying is simple. Browse our current opportunities and submit your application online. You’ll need: an up-to-date CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role to respond to our selection criteria, if requested, demonstrating how your skills and experience align to the role. View current opportunities What to expect - our recruitment process We believe in a recruitment process that’s clear, inclusive, and people focused. Our specialist Talent Acquisition team will support you throughout the journey. Here's what you can expect: Step 1 - Application You’ll receive an email confirming we’ve received your application. Step 2 - Review Our team carefully reviews applications against the role requirements Step 3 - Interview If shortlisted, you’ll be invited to share your experience and learn more about the role. As part of the interview process, we may take references and complete qualification and/or background checks. Step 4 - Offer If successful, we’ll send you a formal offer and guide you through the onboarding process. Step 5 - Prepare to start A member of our team will be available to support you as you get ready to join Adelaide University. We understand moving to a new workplace can be a big change, so we've created some practical tips to help you navigate the transition smoothly. Tips for a successful transition to AU Need adjustments? We’re committed to ensuring our recruitment process is accessible to everyone. If you require adjustments at any stage, please let us know and we’ll work with you to make sure you’re supported. Make a request First Nations Employment Adelaide University aspires to be a university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples and is committed to reconciliation. Our future strategies towards Indigenous advancement include a focus on elevated employment outcomes for First Nations Peoples, with the University’s new Enterprise Agreement including multiple targeted employment benefits and outcomes for First Nations Peoples. As a part of this commitment Adelaide University has a dedicated First Nations Employment Advisor whose role is to provide strategic direction, advise on processes and procedures, support existing staff in their professional development and as a touch point for First Nations people interested in employment opportunities at Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku. For a culturally safe and confidential conversation regarding First Nations Employment at Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku, please contact Alison Hughes, Senior First Nations Employment Advisor at first.nations.employment@adelaide.edu.au Our commitment to you We empower our people to bring their unique contributions to discover, engage and thrive in work that matters. We’re committed to creating a workplace where everyone can succeed. Here’s some of what you’ll find working at Adelaide University: Inclusive culture: We welcome people from all backgrounds and celebrate diversity of thought and experience. Flexibility: Life is dynamic, and we support flexible working to help you thrive. Growth and discovery: From professional development programs to research opportunities, your ambition has room to grow here. Benefits: Enjoy 17% superannuation and a comprehensive program of benefits. Pay and benefits Until a new Adelaide University Enterprise Agreement (EA) is established, employment conditions are guided by foundation university enterprise agreements. Anyone joining us prior to this will be employed under the University of Adelaide Enterprise Agreement or a Senior Staff contract. View University of Adelaide EA View University of South Australia EA Life at Adelaide University Adelaide University stands for progress. We are a university for the future, committed to making a transformative impact on a local and global scale. Our spirit of collective advancement drives future-defining research and innovative teaching that launches rewarding careers. Positive change is at the heart of everything we do. We champion bold ideas that lead to new firsts and significant shifts. Guided by curiosity, we challenge the status quo for a future that is better for all. Whoever you are, wherever you’re from, Adelaide University has the world-class disciplines, people and connections to launch your future. Meet our people At Adelaide University, our people are at the heart of everything we do. Read more about a typical day for people who work here. Thomas, Academic Tutor Meet Thomas Chelsea, Senior Lecturer Meet Chelsea Cameron, Senior Project Officer Meet Cameron Ben, Senior Project Officer Meet Ben Peta, Lecturer Meet Peta Kym, Manager, Marketing and Communications Meet Kym Staff video spotlight se